From: logos-node-android
Subject: [PATCH 0001] Fast replay of the node's own stored blocks at startup

Against logos-blockchain/logos-blockchain tag 0.3.4. Applied with
`git apply -p1` by native/apply-patches.sh. See native/patches/README.md.

At startup the chain service replays every stored block after the LIB, and
each one is verified again in full (leader proof, deferred transaction proofs),
although this node verified it before storing it. With this patch a start
replays those blocks without re-verifying the two proofs, when a marker next to
the database says that this same build already replayed this same database
with full verification. Otherwise (no marker, a new node version or patch set,
a database copied from elsewhere, or LOGOS_REPLAY_VERIFY=full) the start does
a full replay, exactly as upstream, and then writes the marker.

Blocks from the network are verified exactly as before. No change to consensus
rules, wire formats, the database format, the config file or the HTTP API.

